  "final_message": "The kanban board is built, but I haven't built the Docker image or tried the frontend in a browser. I ran the API under gunicorn and checked it with curl. Registering, logging in, creating, moving, deleting, filtering, validation errors, the 401 and the 404 all gave the expected responses. The frontend passes the TypeScript check and `npm run build`.\n\n- **Backend (`backend/app.py`):**\n  - All the endpoints from the spec, with data in SQLite at `data/kanban.db`.\n  - Column positions are renumbered on create, move and delete, so each column always holds 1 to n.\n  - Validation failures return `{\"error\": ..., \"fields\": {...}}` with a 400.\n- **Frontend (`frontend/src/`):** The React/Vite/Tailwind app covers the spec: register and sign-in dialogs, the three columns with counts, the priority filter, drag and drop, and create/edit/delete dialogs. Anyone can view the board; the edit controls only appear when signed in.\n- **Dependencies:** I added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type packages to `frontend/package.json` and updated `package-lock.json`.\n\nThings I added or chose beyond the spec:\n- `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me` endpoints.\n- A `.gitignore`.\n- Passwords must be at least 4 characters and usernames 1\u201364.\n- Tokens expire after 30 days.",
